<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Navarino</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Navarino · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-war-of-independence">Greek War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Navarino was a naval battle fought in 1827 in the bay of Navarino in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> during the Greek War of Independence. A combined British, French and Russian fleet destroyed the Ottoman and Egyptian fleet. The intervention helped secure Greek independence, an early stage in the nationalist movements that progressively dismembered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>'s European territories.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-navarino.jpg" alt="Battle of Navarino" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ambroise Louis Garneray · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Navarino.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
